<title>GREECE: Greek M3 rises provisionally 9.8 pct y/y in Sept.</title>
<headline>Greek M3 rises provisionally 9.8 pct y/y in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek M3 money supply grew provisionally 9.8 percent year-on-year in September from a 9.5 percent in August, overshooting the central bank's 6.0-9.0 percent target range for end-96, the Bank of Greece said in a statement.</p>
<p>The M4 monetary aggregate grew provisionally 7.7 percent year-on-year in September after a 6.7 percent rise in August, it said.  </p>
<p>    M3 money supply		   Sep 96*   Aug 96*    Sep 95</p>
<p>    Stock (in bln drachmas)	 17,224    17,127	15,685</p>
<p>    Yr-on-yr (pct)			9.8	 9.5	  10.3</p>
<p>*  indicates provisional figures</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
